# Architecture map (read first)

`DebuggerApp` (`cmd/gdbforge`) = **composition root / system-context orchestrator**. It wires `backend.Backend`, host-backed `*Ctl` controllers, `Workspace`, MCP/AI, and widgets. Domain logic lives on controllers, not as flat methods on the app alone.

## Roles

| Piece | Role |
|-------|------|
| `DebuggerApp` | Composition root — wires hosts, owns chrome/orchestration |
| `*Ctl` (`breakCtl`, `consoleCtl`, …) | GUI controllers (intents → model → Send / SetItems) |
| `Workspace` | Pane policy above `termui.TabWidget` (marks, placement, layout apply) |
| `backend.Backend` | GDB vs Delve policy; owns the concrete client |
| `internal/mcp` (`GdbMcpService`) | Peer controller (AI) on the same session |
| `core.Session` via `app.GDB()` | Shared session / pipe — not a controller |
| `internal/gdbforge/models` | Shared MVC data (`BreakpointList`, …) owned by ctls |
| `internal/gdbforge/domain` | `DebugDomain` surface for AI / future Lua |
| `internal/gdbforge/widgets`, `internal/termui` | Views only (paint + host intents / callbacks) |

## One shared resource, two controllers

`backend.Backend` is owned by `DebuggerApp` (`-g gdb|dlv`). GUI and AI both use `app.GDB()` (`core.Session`). Widgets never own the session.

## Controllers (`*Ctl`)

| Ctl | Owns | Host iface |
|-----|------|------------|
| `breakCtl` | `BreakpointList`, BP refresh/toggle, gutter paint | `breakHost` |
| `asmCtl` | Assembly widget/list, `preferAsm`/`autoAsm` | `asmHost` |
| `bufferCtl` | per-path `CodeWidget` map (`files`) | `bufferHost` |
| `debugInfoCtl` | threads / call stack | `debugInfoHost` |
| `consoleCtl` | GDB/Delve console submit + paint | `consoleHost` |
| `inferiorIOCtl` | Inferior PTY → OutputWidget | `inferiorHost` |
| `completionCtl` | Wildmenu / completion bar | `completionHost` |
| `searchCtl` | `/` n/N \*/# | — |
| `luaCtl` | Lua panes / jobs | — |
| `dlvCtl` | Delve confirm + frame-nav bookkeeping | — |

`initControllers()` sets each ctl’s host to `*DebuggerApp`. Widget hosts (`BreakpointHost`, `ThreadHost`, …) are also implemented by the app and forward into ctls.

## Where to edit (common)

| Task | Look here first |
|------|-----------------|
| Set/clear BP (Space) | `widgets/code_widget.go` → `breakpoints.go` (`breakCtl`) → `models` |
| BP list e/d | `widgets/breakpoint_widget.go` → `breakCtl` → model |
| Asm BP / `:b asm` / autoAsm | `assembly.go` (`asmCtl`) + `assembly_widget.go` |
| GDB/Delve console submit/paint | `gdb_console.go` (`consoleCtl`) + `widgets/gdb_widget.go` |
| Threads / callstack | `debug_info.go` / `stopped.go` + widgets |
| Pane marks / sticky GDB / layouts | `workspace*.go` (not `TabWidget`) |
| `:b` completions | `buffers.go` (`bufferCtl`) |
| GDB vs Delve policy | `internal/gdbforge/backend` |
| AI / MCP tools | `internal/mcp/tools.go` + `cmd/gdbforge/debug_domain.go` |
| MVC docs | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` § MVC |

## Do not

- Put GDB/`Backend` `Send` / session ownership in widgets
- Duplicate breakpoint truth outside `models.BreakpointList` (on `breakCtl`)
- Put gdbforge pane policy into `termui.TabWidget` (use `Workspace`)
- Treat `gdb.SendCmd` as the MVC controller (it is a transport helper)
- Scatter new `isDLV()` branches — prefer `Backend` methods
